---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Section from "@/components/Section.astro";
import Button from "@/components/Button.astro";
import { profile } from "@/utils/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`Professional background of ${profile.name} — ${profile.title}.`}>
  <Section eyebrow="About" title="Professional Profile">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="prose lg:col-span-2">
        <p>{profile.summary}</p>

        <h3>For academic and research audiences</h3>
        <p>
          My research background spans two research fellowships in Bangladesh's public research
          sector: a Junior Research Fellowship at the Bangladesh Space Research and Remote Sensing
          Organization (SPARRSO, FY2023–FY2025), where I contributed PCB design and firmware to a
          1U CubeSat with a 3D printed carbon fiber composite chassis and to an engineering-model
          CubeSat with a prototype solid propulsion system; and a Research Associate role at the
          Bangladesh Agricultural University Research and Innovation Centre (BAU-RIC, Nov
          2024–Nov 2025), where I led PCB design, firmware, and system design for an AI-based
          harness tag for estrus detection in cattle. That livestock-monitoring work — combining
          TinyML, custom I2C sensor drivers, BLE beacons, and low-power system design for
          continuous field deployment — first at Adorsho PraniSheba and then at BAU-RIC, is the
          clearest throughline in my research interests: getting useful machine intelligence to run
          reliably on power- and connectivity-constrained embedded hardware in the field, not just
          in a lab. I have since applied the same edge-inference and industrial-reliability
          thinking to power-monitoring and predictive-maintenance systems at FronTech. My primary
          direction for graduate research is extending this into embedded systems for e-mobility
          and smart power electronics, informed by leading embedded-systems development on
          electric-vehicle internal systems at Palki Motors.
        </p>
        <p>
          Four of my journal/conference works are listed under Publications, and I hold a B.Sc. in
          Electrical and Electronic Engineering from the University of Dhaka (2018–2022). I am
          actively seeking PhD and M.Sc. research opportunities, as well as collaborations, in
          embedded AI, AIoT, and intelligent power electronics.
        </p>

        <h3>For industry audiences</h3>
        <p>
          I am currently an Embedded Software Engineer (AI) at THT-Space Electrical Company Ltd.,
          building AI-driven embedded solutions for smart home electronics with Wi-Fi/BLE/MQTT
          connectivity, and leading cross-functional firmware and AIoT hardware-software
          integration. Across roles at FronTech, Neways International, Adorsho PraniSheba, and
          ZeronTech BD, I have owned the full stack from schematic and multi-layer PCB design
          (Altium Designer, EasyEDA) through firmware (ESP32, STM32, AVR, MSP430, MicroPython,
          FreeRTOS) to cloud/API integration (AWS IoT Core, Google Cloud IoT, Firebase, MQTT, REST).
        </p>
        <p>
          Representative shipped systems include an IIoT/AIoT predictive-maintenance platform with
          FFT-based fault detection and active power factor correction at FronTech; a multi-device
          fingerprint authentication system with Global Fingerprint Sync and 1:N matching in
          MicroPython at Neways International; and, from independent hardware-portfolio work, a
          smart school-bus safety and tracking system with 20+ operational devices deployed
          since 2023, an edge-AI wearable for cattle estrus detection now in market, an IoT-based
          smart fire-alarm system in market, and an ESP32-based automotive GPS/CAN-bus data logger.
          I lead teams and I am comfortable owning a project end-to-end — architecture, component
          selection, PCB layout, firmware, and field deployment.
        </p>

        <h3>What I work on</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Multi-layer PCB design and hardware bring-up (Altium Designer, EasyEDA)</li>
          <li>Embedded systems &amp; real-time firmware (ESP32, STM32, AVR, MSP430, FreeRTOS, MicroPython)</li>
          <li>IoT / IIoT system architecture and device-to-cloud pipelines (MQTT, CoAP, REST, AWS IoT Core)</li>
          <li>AIoT and Edge AI / TinyML — running inference on constrained hardware</li>
          <li>Power electronics — active power factor correction, EV internal systems, smart power infrastructure</li>
          <li>Industrial automation, predictive maintenance, and machine monitoring systems</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <aside class="space-y-4">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-bg-elevated)] p-5">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)]">
            Currently
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">{profile.currentFocus}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-bg-elevated)] p-5">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)]">
            Open to
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-4 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
            {profile.availableFor.map((a) => <li>{a}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <Button href="/contact" class="w-full">Get in touch</Button>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
